  "name": "Multiplying Two Complex Numbers",
  "problem": "Finally, we can multiply two complex numbers just like multiplying two binomials. Again, we use the fact that $\\mathrm{i}^2=-1.$\n\nSo, to multiply $2 + \\textrm{i}$ and $5 + 3\\textrm{i},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t(2+\\textrm{i})(5+3\\textrm{i}) &= 2 (5+3\\textrm{i})  + \\textrm{i} (5+3\\textrm{i}) \\\n\t\t &= 2\\cdot5 + 2\\cdot(3\\textrm{i}) +\\textrm{i}\\cdot 5+ \\textrm{i} \\cdot (3\\textrm{i}) \\\n\t\t&= 10 + 6\\textrm{i} + 5\\textrm{i} +3\\textrm{i}^2 \\\n\t\t&= 10 + 11\\textrm{i} + 3(-1) \\\n\t\t&= 10 + 11\\textrm{i}  - 3 \\\n\t\t&= 7 + 11\\textrm{i}\n\t}\n$$",
